# Complete semantic translation of the historical standalone usbvc.wlcmd.
#
# Native locklint automatically recognizes all nine historical explicit
# roots through escaped function pointers.  It also recognizes the four
# pseudo-kernel DDI/cb_ops entry points and the strategy/minphys callbacks
# passed to physio().  No explicit root declarations are required.
#
# OSLL produces identical protected-access findings with and without
# "one usbvc_state".  Native locklint distinguishes concrete object
# identities and needs no equivalent declaration for this focused module.
#
# These externally linked functions are module-private helpers, not entries
# from outside the analyzed module.  Other independently discovered root
# reasons remain effective.
declare --external-entry=false usbvc_alloc_map_bufs
declare --external-entry=false usbvc_open_isoc_pipe
declare --external-entry=false usbvc_start_isoc_polling
#
# The historical bus_ops mappings cannot affect usbvc because its dev_ops
# contains no bus_ops vector or call site.
#
# OSLL anchors three multiline assignments at continuation or right-hand-side
# lines while native Sparse anchors them at the assignment starts.  The runner
# normalizes only those accepted source anchors before comparing exact
# source/member pairs.
